{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:simple-eigenpair","title":"def:simple-eigenpair","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":3107,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:simple-eigenpair","uses":[],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:simple-eigenpair","line":5361,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Simple eigenpair]\n\\label{def:simple-eigenpair}\n\n\n\n\nLet $V$ be a finite-dimensional real inner product space. A triple\n$(S,v,\\lambda)$ is a \\emph{simple eigenpair} if $S$ is symmetric, $v\\ne0$,\n$Sv=\\lambda v$, and\n\\[\n\\ker(S-\\lambda\\operatorname{id})=\\operatorname{span}(v).\n\\]\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Simple eigenpair] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a73696d706c652d656967656e70616972\"></span> <p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$V$\">$V$</span> be a finite-dimensional real inner product space. A triple <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(S,v,\\lambda )$\">$(S,v,\\lambda )$</span> is a <em>simple eigenpair</em> if <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S$\">$S$</span> is symmetric, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v\\ne 0$\">$v\\ne 0$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$Sv=\\lambda v$\">$Sv=\\lambda v$</span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\ker (S-\\lambda \\operatorname {id})=\\operatorname {span}(v).  \\]\">\\[  \\ker (S-\\lambda \\operatorname {id})=\\operatorname {span}(v).  \\]</span> ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:lorentz-metric-of-rank-one-distributi